        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/25",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "\"One PR per repository per run\" may conflict with per-session isolation and independent review, because each R004 session produced its own reviewed branch. One large PR raises the human review burden. \"Cannot be reviewed without an earlier unmerged one\" is subjective and hard to test. How section 16 treats PR granularity is not in the supplied evidence.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/26",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "L3 does not say what to do when a change is found on a non-default branch. It names no status other than MERGED_VERIFIED, and no retarget or follow-up PR step, so there is a recovery gap. In 22:30 the controller landed PR #15 on main, but the lesson does not authorize or describe that.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
