        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/27",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Reword the L3 PR rule to: \"Target every PR at the default branch. A stacked PR needs a stated reason in its body, and before handoff it must be retargeted or replaced when its parent merges. Record MERGED_VERIFIED only after the change is on the default branch and the gate passes on a fresh clone of it, with skip counts recorded.\"",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/28",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "L4 (read CI checks before handoff) is justified by the 22:30 failure: CI failed on 575067f with \"The selected orchestrator codex is not available\", while local make test-full, Howl verify and Howl review could not catch it.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/29",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "L4 says nothing about CI that is pending, absent, or unreadable. It does not say the checks must be for the PR head commit. The \"record it in the PR with a reason\" option lets the controller waive a failing check on its own say-so, and the PR body is not a handoff the user is guaranteed to read. The waiver should be limited to failures shown unrelated to the change, with the check named in the handoff message.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/30",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "L4 could consume Howl sessions. R4-S5 was \"6 of 6\", and the 22:30 fix was recorded as repair, not a product session. The lesson does not say whether a CI-fix session counts against the session budget, and the 19A intro says budgets do not change, so the lesson should say to pause when no budget remains and never raise it.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
