  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Overall, the six candidate lines add no permissions, spending or gate removals, and none weakens the no-local-LLM, isolation or human-work rules. Lessons 2, 4 and 6 contain wording that could weaken a gate or conflict with earlier 19A text, listed below.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "prompt-s18",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "prompt-s19a-v4",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 1 (fresh clone before PR) is justified. The 20:54 entry shows a fresh clone catching a manifest-commit drift defect that the working tree hid. The 16:26:38Z entry shows a clean copy catching the ignored `web/data/` problem.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "journal-2026-10-10-20-54-utc",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "journal-2026-10-10t16-26-38z",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The 16:26:38Z entry describes a \"clean copy\", not a `git clone`. The trigger for specifically requiring `git clone` of a commit rests on 20:54, so the trigger note should say so.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "\"Full gate\" in lesson 1 is undefined. The working tree gate showed 0 skipped, but the fresh clone showed 6 data-dependent skips, so skips can hide failures. A clean clone with unexplained skips could be read as a pass.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Lesson 1 wording fix: \"...run the repository's required gate on a fresh `git clone` of the exact commit into a new empty directory; record the commit, pass/fail/skip counts and the reason for any skip. A failure is a finding: no PR until fixed through Howl or paused under section 17.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 1 omits the journal's own candidate check of `git check-ignore` for new output directories. A clone gate only catches this if the gate exercises those files, so the omission is a small coverage gap.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 2 (committed gate script) could weaken the gate. The script is authored in the same session whose work it verifies, so a worker could narrow the script. That conflicts in spirit with the existing 19A rule \"rather than narrowing --verify\" and with the independent-review gate.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
