      "text": "v3_sha256_correctness",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/47",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "ci_pending_or_absent_handling",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/48",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Trigger citations in the v4 lines mix the ISO style (2026-10-10T16:26:38Z) with the \"2026-10-10 20:54 UTC\" style, which matches the journal headings. The v3 rule that heading times come from date -u makes it worth confirming that the minute-resolution headings were generated that way. This is not a defect of the candidate itself.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1/claim/49",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261011-001500-606a90a2e3b1/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "None of the six lines weakens the pause-and-help rule, the no-local-LLM rule, isolation, or public-interface use as written. L1 and L2 could each weaken independent verification through the gaps above, and L1 could invite controller hand-fixes.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
